      "content": "The \"global liberal order\" is not a *good* in the abstract; it is the *practical framework* that allows for human rights and free markets to function, making it the only viable moral baseline for international relations. Strict adherence to sovereignty is a moral shield for tyranny, allowing dictators to violate the rights of their own people without consequence. A non-interventionist stance is morally bankrupt when faced with the clear and present danger of genocide or the spread of totalitarianism.",
      "source": "target",
